{"toolCallId":"call_1d3dbb2ce07e45b090d19f735526c464","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"316:## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n317-\n318-Written for the executing swarm. Follow each rule as written. Where a rule and your own judgment disagree, follow the rule and record the disagreement in `goal.md` section 4.\n319-\n320-### Roles\n321-- **Conductor**: the operator's interactive OpenCode v2 session on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash max. It dispatches workers, runs every verify command, edits only this phase folder, and keeps `goal.md` section 4 current.\n322-- **Worker**: one Task subagent, which inherits the session model. One worker does one lane or one baseline run, then stops.\n323-- **Reviewer**: one read-only frontier review through `cli-codex` at phase close. It writes nothing.\n324-\n325-### Pre-Task Checklist\n326-- [ ] Read this phase's `spec.md`, this plan and `tasks.md` before the first dispatch\n327-- [ ] Read `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md` NEVER rules 1 and 5, which forbid an external CLI dispatch from inside OpenCode, then use the Task tool dispatch below\n328-- [ ] Confirm the working directory is the build worktree recorded in `../goal.md` section 4, never the main checkout\n329-- [ ] Confirm `rg -c 'deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017' opencode.json` prints a number above 0\n330-- [ ] Save every brief to `scratch/briefs/<task-id>.txt` before dispatching it\n331-\n332-### Execution Rules\n333-\n334-| Rule | Requirement |\n335-|------|-------------|\n336-| TASK-SEQ | Run tasks in ID order. Tasks marked `[P]` may run as at most three Task calls in one message, and only when no two write the same file |\n337-| TASK-SCOPE | A worker writes only the paths under ALLOWED WRITE PATHS in its brief |\n338-| TASK-VERIFY | The conductor runs the task's verify command and reads both its output and its exit status before marking the task `[x]` |\n339-| TASK-LOCATE | Find text by its exact content, never by a line number |\n340-| TASK-BANNED | Workers never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git branch`, `git reset`, `git stash`, `generate-context.js` or `/speckit:save` |\n341-\n342-### Worker Brief Skeleton\n343-\n344-Every brief starts with this block, word for word, with the two paths filled in:\n345-\n346-```text\n347-GATE 3 IS PRE-RESOLVED. DO NOT ASK THE DOCUMENTATION-SCOPE QUESTION.\n348-\n349-You are a dispatched Task subagent. This repository's AGENTS.md treats a dispatched worker\n350-as pre-resolved for the spec-folder question, and this prompt is that pre-resolution.\n351-\n352-Your write authority is already bound. The spec folder is:\n353-  specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline\n354-\n355-Proceed directly to the work. Do not print A/B/C/D options. Do not stop to confirm anything.\n356-A failed edit match means a stale anchor: re-read the file and retry; halt only after three\n357-failures on the same file.\n358-Your task is complete only when files exist on disk and the verification command has been run.\n359-\n360-ROLE: You are a read-only auditor. You read files, run read-only commands and write one\n361-result file. Your output is checked line by line by a script.\n362-\n363-ALLOWED WRITE PATHS:\n364-  <the paths this task names>\n365-\n366-BANNED OPERATIONS: git commit, git push, git checkout, git switch, git branch, git reset,\n367-git stash, rm, mv, create.sh outside the task's stated command, generate-context.js,\n368-/speckit:save, and any edit to a file not listed under ALLOWED WRITE PATHS.\n369-```\n370-\n371-The role line is a focused persona summary in place of a full agent file. It is declared here as that small-context exception.\n372-\n373-### Dispatch Command\n374-\n375-```text\n376-Dispatch with the Task tool: subagent_type `general`, description `<TASK id>`, prompt = the full text of\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a3039e","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_23ba519b542a412c81a3887a8556e4e8","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  Level:  3\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 3\n+ PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: No unfilled template placeholders found\n+ TEMPLATE_SOURCE: Template source headers present\n+ ANCHORS_VALID: Anchors well formed in 5 file(s)\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALID: Frontmatter continuity basics present\n+ FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK: All spec-doc frontmatter memory blocks are structurally valid\n+ SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY: All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline\n+ MERGE_LEGALITY: No merge plan supplied; legality check skipped\n+ CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION: No routing payload supplied; contamination check skipped\n+ POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT: No post-save payload supplied; fingerprint check skipped\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT: Graph metadata checked\n+ GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY: Generated metadata passed schema, status-enum and path-prefix invariants\n+ GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT: Generated synopsis fields match the current docs\n+ COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER: No ephemeral comment-hygiene markers found\n+ SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED: Spec status is 'Draft', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\n+ STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY: status cross-doc check not applicable; one status is missing or unclassified\n    - spec.md Status=Draft classified=planned\n    - implementation-summary.md Status=<missing> classified=unknown\n+ AC_COVERAGE: Acceptance coverage gate not active for this level or lifecycle state\n+ TOC_POLICY: TOC policy passed: no TOC headings in non-research spec documents\n+ AI_PROTOCOLS: AI protocols present and complete (4/4)\n+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 3; phases=4, tasks=74, stories=3, scenarios=0)\n+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-recommend-level-quiet-flag' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter values are in the shared list\n+ SOURCE_TAGS: No [SOURCE:] path:line citations in research or review artifacts\n+ GREP_CONVENTION: Grep convention: 5 document(s) conform\n+ LEVEL_MATCH: Level consistent across all files (Level 3)\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT: children_ids matches the on-disk phase children\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY: children_ids entries all carry the packet's own identity\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE: graph-metadata.json shape validation passed\n+ METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY: metadata paths carry the scaffold marker; the packet is not filed yet\n+ DESCRIPTION_SHAPE: description.json shape validation passed\n+ NORMALIZER_LINT: No local normalizeScope*/getOptionalString declarations found outside allowed files\n+ SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY: Spec doc references, metadata, and handover targets resolve cleanly\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED: Canonical-save root-spec check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED: Canonical-save source-doc check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED: save_lineage is present for the refreshed graph metadata\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED: Packet identity normalization drift detected (soft detector)\n    - identity=scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n    - identity=zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS: Description and graph freshness stay within the canonical-save slack window\n+ CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS: Continuity freshness skipped: SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS is not enabled\n    - code:not_opted_in\n+ LINKS_VALID: All wikilinks under the system-spec-kit skill resolve\n\nSummary: Errors: 0  Warnings: 0\n\nRESULT: PASSED\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"295521","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_25023e3f40a84243b1c6fc3f63b2c839","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"001-template-drift-census-and-baseline\n002-template-and-example-defect-repair\n003-versioned-placeholder-gate\n004-template-section-fill-guidance\n005-weak-model-authoring-card\n006-speckit-command-and-agent-alignment\n007-playbook-catalog-readme-alignment\n008-playbook-run-in-worktree\n009-authoring-benchmark-and-closeout\ndescription.json\n---\n---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 1: template-drift-census-and-baseline\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Each task names its verify command, and each dispatched task carries its full worker brief.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"template drift census and baseline tasks\"\n  - \"census lane brief\"\n  - \"baseline authoring run\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 1: template-drift-census-and-baseline\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`, then `Verify:` with the command whose output proves the task.\n\nShell variables used below, set once by the conductor:\n- `WORKTREE`: the build worktree path recorded in `../goal.md` section 4.\n- `PHASE`: `$WORKTREE/specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/001-template-drift-census-and-baseline`\n- `S`: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit`\n- `START`: the commit hash recorded by T003.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Check tools and provider (no file). Verify: `rg -c 'deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017' opencode.json && which jq rg` prints a number above 0 and two paths.\n- [ ] T002 Prove the worktree can validate (no file). Verify: `cd \"$WORKTREE\" && bash $S/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/system-speckit/041-write-recipe-fixes/001-fix-write-recipe-backfill-flag --strict | grep 'RESULT:'` prints `RESULT: PASSED`. When it fails because `node_modules` or `dist` is missing, follow the worktree provisioning in `.skilled/skills/sk-git/SKILL.md` and retry once. When it still fails, STOP the phase.\n- [ ] T003 Record the start state (`goal.md`, `scratch/baseline/status-start.txt`). Run `git -C \"$WORKTREE\" rev-parse HEAD`, write the hash into `goal.md` section 4 as `Start commit`, then run `git -C \"$WORKTREE\" status --porcelain > \"$PHASE/scratch/baseline/status-start.txt\"`, then run the spec-kit suite once with `npm --prefix \"$WORKTREE/$S\" test > \"$PHASE/scratch/baseline/suite-start.txt\" 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\" >> \"$PHASE/scratch/baseline/suite-start.txt\"`. Phases 2 to 5 compare their suite runs with this file. Verify: `grep -c 'Start commit' \"$PHASE/goal.md\"` prints `1`, and `tail -1 \"$PHASE/scratch/baseline/suite-start.txt\"` prints an `exit=` line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 [P] Dispatch census lanes A, B and C (`scratch/ledger/lane-a.jsonl`, `lane-b.jsonl`, `lane-c.jsonl`). Write one brief per lane to `scratch/briefs/T004-A.txt`, `T004-B.txt` and `T004-C.txt`, each made of the skeleton in `plan.md` section AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL followed by the lane text below, then make three Task calls in one message, one per lane, with the plan's dispatch rule, writing each reply to `scratch/runs/T004-A.txt`, `T004-B.txt` and `T004-C.txt`. Verify: `for l in a b c; do jq -c . \"$PHASE/scratch/ledger/lane-$l.jsonl\" > /dev/null && echo \"lane-$l JSON_OK\"; done` prints three `JSON_OK` lines.\n\n  Lane text, with `<LANE>`, `<PATHS>` and `<OUT>` filled from this table:\n\n  | LANE | PATHS | OUT |\n  |------|-------|-----|\n  | A | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/` except its `examples/` folder | `scratch/ledger/lane-a.jsonl` |\n  | B | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/examples/` | `scratch/ledger/lane-b.jsonl` |\n  | C | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/` and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md` | `scratch/ledger/lane-c.jsonl` |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6cac96","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
